The GPU to GPU demo, with its regions on the CPU, when node B never answers: node
A reports the timeout and stops at the first round, then so does node B.

RUN: rm -rf %t.src && mkdir -p %t.src
RUN: sed 's/send(ToA, Sum, !IO)/true/; s/after(10000)/after(300)/' %S/../../examples/gpu-to-gpu/gpu_to_gpu.m > %t.src/gpu_to_gpu.m
RUN: cp %S/../../examples/gpu-to-gpu/demo_node.m %t.src/
RUN: not make -s -C %S/../../examples run-gpu-to-gpu-cpu MERKC=merkc BUILD=%t O=0 PORT=47102 GPU_SOURCES="%t.src/gpu_to_gpu.m %t.src/demo_node.m" > %t.out
RUN: grep "^.[nG]\|^error" %t.out | sort -s -k1,2 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

CHECK:[GPU A] sending numbers, each 1
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] got this many numbers: 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[GPU B] sending back their sum 1000
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] connecting to node B at 127.0.0.1:{{[0-9]+}}
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] found node B's mailboxes
CHECK-NEXT:[node A] round 1
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] listening on port {{[0-9]+}}
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] node A has connected
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] round 1
CHECK-NEXT:[node B] round 2
CHECK-NEXT:error: GPU A waiting for the sum: nothing arrived in time
CHECK-NEXT:error: GPU B waiting for the numbers: nothing arrived in time
CHECK-NOT:{{.}}
